    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1432">

                <pb facs="1536" n="1522" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Peru/1110: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-06T19:00:00-04:00">April 6, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>361. Your 461, April 4. The Department does not believe it would be desirable to
                    use the new rotenone proposal to bargain for debt settlements.</p>
                <p>Further, since the proposed prices for rotenone are thought to be necessary to
                    obtain badly needed supplies, the new offer contained in the Department’s 305,
                    March 24 and 341, April l,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d1432-f1"/> should be made
                    rather promptly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
